 "brief": "Create a single hollow 3D-printable lower-leg part, 330 mm tall, shaped like a human calf and shin: broad and rounded near the upper calf, bulging slightly backward, tapering gradually into a narrow ankle, with a gently curved front shin surface and smooth anatomical contours. Upper cross-section 115 \u00d7 105 mm, lower 85 \u00d7 80 mm, with 8 mm walls. Add a 210 \u00d7 60 mm rectangular opening on the back with six 4.5 mm mounting holes for a removable lid. Add reinforced 12 mm-thick hinge tabs at the top and bottom, each extending 37.5 mm beyond the body with a centered 8.5 mm pivot hole running left to right.",
